    "title": "Vikings to entertain trade offers for Jonathan Greenard - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt Hanifan ,\n10 hours ago Vikings to entertain trade offers for Jonathan Greenard Days ahead of the new league year, the Minnesota Vikings are entertaining trade offers for All-Pro EDGE rusher Jonathan Greenard , ESPN NFL insider Adam Schefter first reported Tuesday morning.\nSchefter noted that, while Minnesota would prefer to keep Greenard, who’s been one of the NFC’s most productive pass rushers the last two seasons, it is trying to find ways to duck below the salary cap, which they entered the month north of $40 million over.\nYou could argue that Greenard is the Vikings’ best defensive player entering 2026. He was limited to just 12 games last year, totaling three sacks. Though he logged 22 pressures with 12 hurries and 12 QB hits in 2025. In 2024, he had 59 tackles, 18 tackles-for-loss, 12 sacks and 42 pressures.\nAccording to Over The Cap, trading Greenard pre-June 1 would save the Vikings $12.3 million. He is expected to have a $22.2 million cap hit with a $18.4 million base salary.\nGreenard’s price isn’t going to come cheap — likely at the cost of multiple picks, including at least one first- or second-rounder — given his age and production. While he’s battled injuries, he’s 28-years-old and has developed into a pretty impactful pass rusher.\nVikings expected to release Aaron Jones, Javon Hargrave Selling high — or, at the very least, lukewarm (given his 2025 season) — isn’t a bad move by the Vikings, should they get some decent draft equity. Minnesota still has Andrew Van Ginkel and third-year EDGE rusher Dallas Turner , who filled in amicably in the second half of the season. Turner had eight sacks and four forced fumbles in 17 games (10 starts).\nWhat would you give up for Greenard? Let us know in the comments below!\n***\nSubscribe to Vendetta’s Twitch\nSubscribe to Vendetta’s YouTube\nCheck out Vendetta Fantasy Contests\nClick here for more NFL content\nThe post Vikings to entertain trade offers for Jonathan Greenard appeared first on Vendetta Sports Media .",
    "summary": "10 hours ago Vikings to entertain trade offers for Jonathan Greenard Days ahead of the new league year, the Minnesota Vikings are entertaining trade offers for All-Pro EDGE rusher Jonathan Greenard , ESPN NFL insider Adam Schefter first reported Tuesday morning. Schefter noted that, while Minnesota would prefer to keep Greenard, who’s been one of the NFC’s most productive pass rushers the last two seasons, it is trying to find ways to duck below the salary cap, which they entered the month north of $40 million over.",
